# Canonical Turtle for the protocol-derived encoding of:
#   Matthias Holzenkamp et al. (2025). Evaluation of uncertainty estimations for Gaussian process regression based machine learning interatomic potentials.
#   Machine Learning Science and Technology. doi:10.1088/2632-2153/ae09ef  arXiv:2410.20398v2
#
# Version read: arxiv-preprint arXiv:2410.20398v2 (sha256 1bd165f7e4495b28...);
#   the DOI above is cited, numbers are those of the version read.
# Corpus rank 365 (Training/reliability). Method identity follows
#   artifacts/kg/METHODS.md (registry: artifacts/kg/methods-registry.csv).
# Generated by artifacts/scripts/encode_paper.py from artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/holzenkamp2025.yaml.
#
# Encoding scope: the study record only. The models are exact
# (non-sparse) GPyTorch Gaussian-process regressors with ARD Gaussian
# kernels on unsorted Coulomb matrices or on DScribe SOAP (rcut 5 A,
# nmax 3, lmax 1) for energies of rMD17 benzene and aspirin and WS22 SMA
# and O-HBDI, and for TD-LC-DFTB excitation energies of porphyrin. No
# registry method matches GPR on Coulomb matrices, and the paper does not
# present the SOAP model as GAP, so no MLIP run is encoded (decision
# wanted). All errors (calibration curves, reliability diagrams and
# uncertainty-sampling MAE curves) are figure-only.

